<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="68936" href="schedule/2017/fall/ACE/592/68936.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2017" href="schedule/2017.xml">2017</calendarYear><term id="120178" href="schedule/2017/fall.xml">Fall 2017</term><subject id="ACE" href="schedule/2017/fall/ACE.xml">Agricultural and Consumer Economics</subject><course id="592" href="schedule/2017/fall/ACE/592.xml">Special Topics</course></parents><sectionNumber>EM </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Empirical Methods</sectionTitle><sectionDateRange>Meets 23-Oct-17 - 13-Dec-17.</sectionDateRange><creditHours>2 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course is an introduction to recent methodological developments in empirical microeconomics.  We will begin by learning about topics related to the design of randomized control trials, including power calculations, stratified randomization, spatial spillovers, random encouragement designs, measurement issues and the Hawthorne effect, selective trials, and pre-analysis plans.  Discussions on standard error adjustments for spatial and temporal correlation.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>B</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2017-10-23Z</startDate><endDate>2017-12-13Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>01:30 PM</start><end>02:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MW     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>313</roomNumber><buildingName>Mumford Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Crost" firstName="B">Crost, B</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>